Z||000005||West Coast Fiero||12-29-2001||05:08 PM||||rememeber, some thought the PT Cruiser was going to bomb ( because of retro styling ), but it was well recieved by the public which made Ford get on the ball and come out with an updated Thunder Bird, as well as possibly the Ford 49 ( I greatly dislike Ford, but I would not hesitate to buy a 49, not for a second )<P> But Im not really sure if the SSR is GM's answer to all the retro designs in production, granted it does resemble early 50's trucks with the front fenders and grille, but I have no idea what the whole convertable idea is about.<P> More than likely it will be powered by the 5.3 ( 327 ) which is allready in use in the Avelanche and other GM trucks. The engine has all ready recieved a wide negative view from publications such as Car and Driver, Peterson's 4 wheel and Off Road, Fourwheeler, and SUV Magazine.<P> I love the idea that GM wants to proceed with new ideas and concepts, but c'mon - the Aztec, really - what the hell was that all about. Avelanche - very great idea of the convert-a-cab system, but who would by a plastic truck with the intentions of using it as a <I>truck</I>.<P> But you have to see the SSR for what it is, a factory lowered, convertable, sleek <I>truck</I> - I beleive it will sell....<P> <B>JUST GET RID OF THE DAMN 5.3!!!</B><BR>hehehe<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://clubs.hemmings.com/fieroswest/WestCoast300.gif"> <BR>Eric Nelson<BR>Technician,<BR>West Coast Fiero<BR>www.cwestco.com<BR>310-305-4111||||reg||1
