Z||000014||GTFiero1||12-29-2001||08:17 PM||||you have to see it in person to appreciate it. i saw it at the philadelphia auto show last year and it looks great. its suppose to have 2 engine options, one with 280hp and the other with 300hp but engine options are expected in the nea future. everybody thinks it suppose to be chevy's good lookin answer to the ugly lightning, but its not. Chevy said that itwas never intended to be, it was to be in a class by itself. its ment to be just a nice weekend cruiser. The reason wh they used a truck as a hot rod is because no one did it yet and thy could do a lot more with it due to lesser inspection restrictions. This is all in one of the recent GM High Performance magazines.<P>------------------<BR>Adam J. B.<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fiero_3.jpg">   <BR>you gotta keep on keepin on...<BR>IM AOL: GTFiero &  Rumpdetective (dont ask)||||reg||1
