Z||000018||BAM-BAM||12-30-2001||11:43 AM||||  I give it a big thumbs up! I have always liked the Retro look. Dodge did it, Ford did it and now Chevrolet. I also heard on the radio the other day the Chevy plans on a 50's series retro project involving the Belair. Now that will be bang'n. Hope to see it come true.<BR>  After all isn't that what most of us do to the Fiero? I mean, we are always improving the handling, power and ergonomics. We have the first "Retro Mid-engine commuter/sports car ever manufactured in mass quantities and continually changing and upgrading in America". That should solve the argument in the other thread <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">(Sorry TRIAD, I couldn't resist)<BR>  Here's some pics of the SSR.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ChevySSR.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ChevySSR2.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ChevySSR3.jpg"> <P>I like it. I like it a lot  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_watchout.gif"><P><BR>Peace, B2 OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_watchout.gif"><BR>||||reg||14
Z||000019||Mickey_Moose||12-30-2001||12:29 PM||||Personally..I like it myself, ONLY as long as you keep the top down - top up it looks like an AMC pacer with a truck box  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I will sell, but to a limited market as did the Prowler, I don't think it is really meant as a truck to haul a wack of lumber or gravel  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>...but hell if they dropped in a 400+ hp 427 big block or similar, I may be interested in buying one after all there is not much point (in my books) to spend $30k on something and them droping in another $5k to make it into something good :P<P>Tim<BR>||||reg||1
